{# Generic dialog hull for every add, edit, cancel and confirm surface. It fills
   the page `overlay` slot and owns only the hull: a title row, then `message`,
   `body` and `actions`. The confirmation rule these surfaces obey is written in
   designbook/design-system/action-pattern.md — a confirmation is THIS component
   with prose in `body` and two actions, not a second component.

   The state is the `<dialog>` element's own `open` attribute, rendered from the
   `open` prop — the accessible state, never a CSS class. That is what makes the
   open and closed states readable with JavaScript disabled entirely.

   The head's breadcrumb is a SLOT, not text, because context is a control now
   (spec D15). Drupal derives "what can be added here" from the route, which is why
   the first version of this pattern refused to create without a project in scope;
   Linear instead carries the context IN the dialog — its own create dialog has both
   a `Set team` button and a `Change project` combobox — pre-filled from wherever you
   came from and changeable on the spot. So the `bakers.build ›` segment is a picker with the
   same grammar as a property pill, and the four-step resolution that fills it is
   written in designbook/design-system/action-pattern.md. It stays out of the `body`
   deliberately: it is context, not a field, which is what keeps the pill row from
   growing a fifth pill.

   `message` is rendered ABOVE `body` deliberately: a form-level refusal has to
   appear where the writer is looking, not below the fields it complains about.

   The hull CENTERS ITSELF, and that positioning belongs here rather than to the
   page: `shell`'s overlay slot is a plain region at the end of the shell's flex
   row, so a `<dialog open>` left in normal flow lays out beside the sidebar and
   pushes the shell's chrome aside. `fixed` plus a centred translate is what
   makes it read as an overlay — and it is the dialog's own concern, because
   `shell` must keep working for any other overlay content.

   Runtime modality is STILL not here, and that half is unchanged: `open` renders
   the element in the normal flow of the top layer's absence, and the real top
   layer, the focus trap and ::backdrop exist only after showModal(), so there is
   deliberately no scrim — a painted one would claim a modality this markup does
   not have.

   Esc AND THE CLOSE BUTTON ARE WIRED, though, and this docblock claimed the
   opposite for longer than it was true — it said they "belong to the ticket that
   makes these dialogs interactive" and that the close button "carries a data
   hook and no handler", which was already false in the commit that added the
   handler. Both are `island`'s: `island/js/island.dialog.js` closes on a
   `[data-dialog-close]` click and on Escape, and this component reaches it by
   declaring `island/dialog` as a library dependency rather than by shipping a
   script of its own — SDC's `replaces:` swaps the component and not its library,
   so the dependency has to be stated here. The data hooks this template renders
   (`data-dialog` on the element, `data-dialog-close` on the button) are that
   file's documented contract, so they are markup with a reader now.

   What "close" MEANS is deliberately not this component's decision: island
   returns to whatever `[data-dialog-cancel]` inside the hull points at, which
   the form in the body renders — in place when that is the current screen. A hull whose content offers no such control
   simply cannot be closed by the button, and that is the content's business.

   The width is 720px because the pill row is what sets it. The peer pills
   carrying real values — a parent ticket's title is the long one — need about
   700px to stay on ONE row, which is what the
   grammar's rule 3 asks for and what the Linear dialogs it was read off measure;
   at the first iteration's 560px the row wrapped as soon as a parent ticket's
   title appeared in it. `max-w-[90vw]` keeps that honest on a narrow viewport,
   where wrapping is the correct outcome rather than a defect.

   Slot wrappers live OUTSIDE their {% block %} so filling a slot replaces the
   content and never the wrapper. `message` and `actions` are captured first and
   tested for content, so an {% embed %} that fills only the block still gets its
   wrapper (the same idiom `section` uses for its header). #}
{% set dialog_id = id|default('bakers-dialog') %}
{% set title_id = dialog_id ~ '__title' %}
{% set context_content %}{% block context %}{% if context %}{{ context }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set message_content %}{% block message %}{% if message %}{{ message }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set actions_content %}{% block actions %}{% if actions %}{{ actions }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{# Keep dialog controls above Drupal administration toolbars, including in short viewports. #}
<dialog{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'dialog', 'fixed', 'left-1/2', 'top-1/2', '-translate-x-1/2', '-translate-y-1/2', 'z-1000',
    'w-[720px]', 'max-w-[90vw]', 'max-h-[90vh]', 'overflow-y-auto', 'p-0', 'rounded-md',
    'border', 'border-border', 'bg-surface', 'text-text', 'shadow-lg',
  ]) }}
  id="{{ dialog_id }}"
  data-dialog
  {#- The accessible name: `aria-labelledby` points at the visible title, and
      `label` REPLACES it when the name must differ from what is on screen.
      They are mutually exclusive on purpose — emitting both would leave
      `aria-label` dead, because `aria-labelledby` wins the name computation. -#}
  {%- if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% else %} aria-labelledby="{{ title_id }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if open %} open{% endif %}>
  <div class="dialog__head flex items-center gap-[8px] h-[44px] px-[16px] border-b border-border-2">
    {%- if context_content|trim is not empty %}
      <div class="dialog__context flex items-center gap-[8px] shrink-0">
        {{ context_content }}
        <span class="dialog__separator text-text-faint" aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    <h2 id="{{ title_id }}" class="dialog__title flex-1 min-w-0 truncate m-0 text-heading font-bold text-title">{{ title }}</h2>
    {%- if dismissible %}
      {{ include('bb_theme:button', {
        label: 'Close dialog',
        variant: 'ghost',
        icon_only: true,
        icon: include('bb_theme:icon', { name: 'x-circle', size: 'sm' }, with_context = false),
        attributes: create_attribute().setAttribute('data-dialog-close', true),
      }, with_context = false) }}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {%- if message_content|trim is not empty %}
    <div class="dialog__message px-[16px] pt-[14px] [&_.message]:mb-0">{{ message_content }}</div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="dialog__body flex flex-col gap-4 px-[16px] py-[14px]">{% block body %}{% if body %}{{ body }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}</div>
  {%- if actions_content|trim is not empty %}
    <div class="dialog__actions flex items-center justify-end gap-[8px] px-[16px] py-[12px] border-t border-border-2">{{ actions_content }}</div>
  {% endif %}
</dialog>
